{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Each by his standard, with signs.</b> On the standards were inscribed letters of the names of the patriarchs. And how were they inscribed? On the standard of Reuven: אי״י; on the second: בצ״ע; on the third: רח״ק; on the fourth: מק״ב. The first letters of these words form אברם, the second letters יצחק, the third letters יעקב. And the cloud spread over Israel in the shape of the letter ה of אברהם. Another interpretation: <b>with signs for their fathers' houses</b> — the figure of a man on Reuven's standard, dyed with the color of אדם, set in the breastplate for his tribe, a sign for the mandrakes (דודאים) that he found, for they resemble the form of a man. The figure of a lion on Yehuda's standard, for he was called a lion, dyed with the color of נפך. The figure of an ox on Efraim's standard, for his father was called an ox, dyed with the color of שוהם. The figure of an eagle on Dan's standard, dyed with the color of לשם. And the Tabernacle was in the middle, alluding to the holy creatures that form the four faces of the throne of glory, and from them the kingdoms learned to have maps painted in various colors."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:16.796841966Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}